Usage: virtualhost.sh <domain> [options]

Manage Apache2 Virtual Hosts - V1.0

Arguments:
  <domain>             The domain name for the virtual host (e.g. example.com)

Options:
  -p <path>            Set the root directory for the virtual host (required when creating a site)
  -d                   Delete the specified virtual host
  -h                   Display this help and exit

Description:
  This script simplifies the creation and deletion of Apache2 virtual hosts.
  When creating a new virtual host, it will:
    - Generate the configuration file in /etc/apache2/sites-available/
    - Enable the site using a2ensite
    - Restart Apache2
    - Prompt for backup if an existing config is found

  When deleting a virtual host, it will:
    - Disable the site using a2dissite
    - Ask whether to remove the configuration file
    - Restart Apache2

Examples:
  sudo ./virtualhost.sh example.com -p /var/www/example
      Create a new virtual host for example.com with the specified root directory.

  sudo ./virtualhost.sh example.com -d
      Delete the virtual host for example.com.

  ./virtualhost.sh -h
      Show this help message.

Notes:
  - This script must be run as root (use sudo).
  - Make sure to update your /etc/hosts file for local testing.

